erral center — don’t turn to scalpers"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/24-04"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["04"]},"Before seeking medical care outside your home province, ask locally first — the need for such care should ideally be assessed by an associate chief physician or higher"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/24-05"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["05"]},"Stop treating tertiary hospitals as mere prescription hubs — stable chronic disease patients should turn to primary care"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/24-06"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["06"]},"If you have doubts about treatment, request to seal the medical records on the spot; both parties must be present, a list must be drawn up, and each side gets a copy"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/24-07"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["07"]},"After every medical visit, keep a personal copy of your medical records, test reports, and imaging scans"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/24-08"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["08"]},"Even without money or ID, and unable to identify yourself, emergency care must be provided first"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/24-09"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["09"]},"Disability assessments must be conducted only after treatment is complete; doing it too early results in a lower rating"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/24-10"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["10"]},"After treatment, functional impairments may indeed remain; apply for a disability certificate at the county-level disability association in your hukou area"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/24-11"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["11"]},"Thank the doctors who saved you — send thank-you letters, banners, or satisfaction ratings instead of cash gifts. The rules prohibit money, not gratitude"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/24-12"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["12"]},"Before getting a dental implant, ask what the package price includes; prioritize providers committed to price regulation, and do not trust low-price ads"]}]}]},{"tag":"div","props":{"className":"life-tip-page"},"children":[{"tag":"nav","props":{"className":"life-tip-breadcrumb","aria-label":"Breadcrumb"},"children":[{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/book"},"children":["Explore the book"]},{"tag":"span","props":{"aria-hidden":"true"},"children":["/"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/book/24"},"children":["Chapter 24"," ·"," ","Seeking medical care: How to save money and avoid unnecessary hassle"]}]},{"tag":"article","props":{"className":"life-entry-card status-unmarked is-standalone","id":"24-01"},"children":[{"tag":"div","props":{"className":"life-entry-top"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{"className":"life-entry-number"},"children":["01"]},{"tag":"span","props":{"className":"life-evidence grade-a"},"children":["Evidence"," ","A"]}]},{"tag":"h1","props":{"lang":"en"},"children":["For common illnesses, patients should first visit community clinics; referrals then proceed stepwise to larger hospitals, after which the hospital deductible is calculated only once"]},{"tag":"p","props":{"lang":"en","className":"life-entry-summary"},"children":["Start by going to a community clinic, which will then refer you to a larger hospital for inpatient care. The amount you pay out-of-pocket at the start is counted only once. If you go directly to a tertiary hospital for admission and later return to a community clinic for recovery, you might have to pay that amount twice. However, if a larger hospital refers you back to a community clinic for continued treatment, the deductible is not recalculated for the same condition during that period."]},{"tag":"div","props":{"className":"life-entry-impact"},"children":[{"tag":"div","props":{},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["Cost"]},{"tag":"p","props":{},"children"